skill: profile-optimization
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for profile-optimization. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[9]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-profile, Optimize my Instagram profile — I'm a solo founder building a SaaS social scheduler., "reads brand-profile, voice, audience, and social-strategy first|applies the 3-second clarity test (who you help, what you offer, why follow) above the fold|uses the searchable name field for a niche keyword, not just the name|writes a who/what/why bio with a clear CTA within the platform's character limit|matches the link to the current goal and specs pinned posts + highlights|delivers a ready-to-apply spec and frames itself as advisory (doesn't claim to edit the profile via WoopSocial)"
  - clarity-over-clever-pushback, My bio is 'Dream big ✨ | coffee lover ☕ | living my best life 🌴' — polish it up., "pushes back that the bio is vague and doesn't say who it helps, what it does, or why to follow|rewrites it for clarity first (who/what/why) while keeping personality and voice|explains a visitor decides in seconds and confusion loses the follow"
  - use-searchable-fields, "For the name field I'll just put my name, and on LinkedIn my headline is just 'Founder'.", "explains the Instagram name field is searchable/indexed and the LinkedIn headline is prime SEO real estate|recommends adding a niche keyword (what you do / who you help), not just the name or title|gives a concrete example like 'Name | what they do'"
  - link-cta-match, I have one Linktree with 15 links and a 'link in bio' CTA. Good enough?, advises matching the link to the current goal/CTA rather than a cluttered hub of 15 links|recommends a single clear destination (or a tidy hub leading with the priority action) and a specific reason to click|ties the link choice to the strategy's primary goal
  - niche-not-everyone, I want my profile to appeal to everyone so I get the most followers., pushes back that a profile for everyone converts no one|recommends a specific niche/positioning so the right visitor instantly self-identifies|ties this to clarity and the 3-second test
  - banner-brief-not-stock, For my LinkedIn banner I'll just use a generic stock photo of a city., "treats the banner/header as prime real estate that should carry a value prop, proof, or CTA|provides a banner brief (what it should communicate visually) rather than a generic image|keeps it on-brand"
  - advisory-not-bridge, Just update my bio and profile picture directly., "clarifies it can't edit profile fields via WoopSocial (which publishes posts/media, not profile changes)|produces a ready-to-paste spec for the user to apply in each app|does not claim to have made the change"
  - new-account-no-proof-and-voice, "Write my bio but I'm brand new with no followers, results, or testimonials.", "uses clarity, specificity, and a sharp niche instead of fabricated proof or vanity metrics|does not invent fake numbers, clients, or testimonials|stays on-voice (no exclamation marks or hype words)"
  - no-analytics-claims, Which bio version performs best for us?, "does not claim WoopSocial provides profile analytics|points to native profile insights the user pulls (profile visits, link taps, follows) or qualitative review (does it pass the 3-second test)|frames bio testing as something to observe, not data it can supply"
